{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>I will incline</b> — I will speak this wisdom by way of parable, such as: \"they will not see light\" (Psalms 49:20), \"like sheep they are set for Sheol\" (Psalms 49:15). And because the riddle is hidden and sealed, therefore I will open it." "<b>And the meaning of \"upon a harp\"</b> — for this psalm is sung with it. And it is possible that the meaning of \"I will incline\" is: I too will incline my ear to the parable. And the meaning: I will also reprove my own soul."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The verse fragments cited are from the same psalm (49:20, 49:15), not external references."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:14.365583406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}